{% from "guide/macros.njk" import params, files, note %}

{% set ex = "validation-states" %}{% set exTitle = "Agree, disagree, not reviewed" %}{% include "guide/example.njk" %}

<h2 class="g-h2" id="usage">Usage</h2>
<div class="g-prose">
  <p>Put the mark directly after the pill it judges. In the lists it renders only when <code>flags.validation</code> is on, which also adds the Validation section to the filter menus:</p>
  <p><code>{{ "{% if flags.validation %}{{ validationDot(row.validation, row.expert_treatment) }}{% endif %}" }}</code></p>
  <p>The mark reviews a classification, not a legal conclusion. The published site is built without it.</p>
</div>

<h2 class="g-h2" id="parameters">Parameters</h2>
{{ params([
  ["state", "\"agree\" | \"disagree\" | other", "", "<code>agree</code> draws a blue check, <code>disagree</code> a purple cross, anything else a grey question mark."],
  ["expert_treatment", "string", "\"\"", "The expert's own label when they disagree; it joins the tooltip and the accessible name."]
]) }}

<h2 class="g-h2" id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<div class="g-prose"><p>The mark is <code>role="img"</code> with a full <code>aria-label</code> ("Invalidated by expert. Expert classification: Distinguished by") and is focusable so its tooltip opens from the keyboard (<code>tooltips.js</code>, through <code>data-tooltip</code>).</p></div>

